From dbd4b16e5776213cd9fc9585ebefc6cd93d5bb4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <jelon@tbu.net>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 17:22:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 009/206] feat(shorebird): reproduce class table link info --
 byte-identical to theirs

Implements --print_class_table_link_info_to and
--print_class_table_link_debug_info_to. Both outputs are byte-for-byte
identical to Shorebird's own gen_snapshot on the same kernel (31416 bytes
binary, 36761 bytes JSON, verified with cmp).

The hash encoding was recovered rather than guessed. Decompiling their
GetClassTableLinkInfo showed the call chain Class::Handle -> String::ScrubName
-> Utils::StringHash -> std::to_string, and the data confirmed the shape:
stripping the last digit puts all 606 values below 2^32 (only 62 fit otherwise),
and the three classes whose suffix is 2 are exactly the three duplicate scrubbed
names -- Function (cid 7 and 598), Symbol (308, 521), _UnmodifiableMapMixin
(384, 432) -- each sharing a hash body with its cid-1 twin. So:

  hash = str(Utils::StringHash(ScrubName(name))) + str(nth_occurrence)

Placed under runtime/vm/shorebird/ to match their own layout, which their
binaries' assertion strings and dSYM reveal as runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc.

Also fixes a long-standing build defect inherited from the 3.7 branch:
sim_bridge.cc, sim_bridge_arm64.S and sim_transition.{cc,h} were registered in
vm_sources_tests rather than vm_sources, so the A2/C1 simulator bridge was only
ever compiled into run_vm_tests and was ABSENT from gen_snapshot and every
production artifact. That is why InvokeWithTHR/CallHostFunction/ShorebirdSimToCpu
could not be found in the linked binary earlier -- not inlining, just never
built. Only *_test.cc remain in the test list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

